system "DIN:nog-Cyrl:Latn:1460-2-2011" {

metadata {
  authority_id din
  id 1460-2-2011-44
  language iso-639-3:nog
  source_script Cyrl
  destination_script Latn
  name "DIN 1460-2:2011-10, Tabelle 1 row 44: Nogaisch (Turkic)"
  url https://www.beuth.de/de/norm/din-1460-2/134564104
  creation_date 2011
  adoption_date
  description {
    DIN 1460-2:2011-10, Romanization of Cyrillic alphabets of
    non-Slavic languages, Tabelle 1, language row 44
    (Nogaisch). The table assigns each Cyrillic letter of the
    language's alphabet a Latin letter or letter group; the column
    order follows DIN 1460:1982 (Slavic). Extracted mechanically from
    the standard's text layer; the mapping rows below are the table's
    own cells.
  }

  notes {
    note "Extraction provenance: the PDF's text layer carries the full
    grid; columns were anchored on the per-page position-number row and
    each cell matched by x-coordinate to its Cyrillic header letter.
    Position 13's header glyph is PUA (U+E519) in the text layer and
    was visually identified at 10x as h with comma below (U+0068 + U+0322), the plain-h counterpart of position 12's hooktop-h symbol."
  }
}

tests {
   "a" ->  "a"
   "б" ->  "b"
   "в" ->  "v"
   "г" ->  "g"
# Exhaustive per-row tests for din-nog-Cyrl-Latn-1460-2-2011, generated from the source
# document's table.
# Source: DIN 1460-2:2011-44, Tabelle 1, language row 44 (Nogaisch); held
# source interscript-private-references/din/din-1460-2.pdf. Rows are the
# language column's printed cells. The printed grid (pymupdf find_tables
# re-extraction of the Tabelle pages, 2026-11-26) is authoritative for every
# cell; the durable #242 mechanical extraction tools/din1460-2-table.json
# (x-anchored text layer) supplies the position-number headers. Every
# printed cell of this row was verified against rendered grid crops.
# Supplementary columns 91-99 (this batch's extraction): the #242 extraction
# stops at position 90; the printed grid's columns 91-99 are transcribed
# here from the grid. Correction table (text layer -> print): position 96's
# header is printed Cyrillic ya while the #242 artifact stores Latin 'ja'
# (the lookalike-glyph defect documented in the odni batch-1 artifacts);
# rows 25/62 position 94 print a-grave (à) where the text layer stores
# a-dot-above (ȧ); the t/n-cedilla targets the grid text layer precomposes
# (ņ/ţ) are transcribed decomposed (n + U+0327 / t + U+0327), the DIN
# cedilla series whose other cells are decomposed in the text layer and
# whose printed marks were visually verified as cedillas. Parenthesised
# cells are DIN's optional-value notation, transcribed paren-stripped.
# Generated tests cover the 33 passing rows of 33; the map's own hand tests
# are retained (duplicated froms are the batch-2 convention).
# Provenance artifact: scripts/row-sources/din-nog-Cyrl-Latn-1460-2-2011.json (33 rows).
# generated-by: maps/scripts/gen-row-tests.mjs (2026-11-25); regenerate from the artifact, do not hand-edit.
